WEBVTT

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.610
Gama Gama is gone.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:18.040
So I...

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:28.920
I thought I was trying really hard at work.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.960
Now I don't have the drive anymore.

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:33.850
Yeah.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.880
Sorry, I'm the worst.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.550
I'm causing so much trouble.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.020
I'm really sorry.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:54.390
Fuuka...

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:57.530
<b>Kamehausu</b>

00:02:58.210 --> 00:02:59.820
Good morning.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.380
Good morning, Kukuru-chan.

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:05.610
Thank you for everything, Misaki-san.

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:07.330
I'll leave on the afternoon ferry tonight.

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.640
I haven't done anything.

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:12.330
You have your friend to thank 
for coming to get you.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:16.020
I knew I couldn't stay forever.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:18.590
Fuuka helped me clear my mind.

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:24.360
Having something positive to say means 
you've charged up the energy to run forward again.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:27.160
Don't push yourself too hard, though.

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:28.850
Are you Umi-yan-san's...

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:30.480
Guden Misaki.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:32.590
Miyazawa Fuuka.

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:35.110
We're in Umi-yan-san's care.

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:38.280
Likewise, thank you 
for taking care of Gou-chan.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:43.240
Misaki-san does university research 
and conservation of sea turtles.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:44.410
Conservation?

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:46.680
Are you aware that loggerhead sea turtles

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:49.540
and leatherback sea turtles are classified 
as endangered species?

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:51.530
I've heard about it.

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:56.240
My department is investigating 
sea turtle biology and behavior.

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:59.950
We're trying to keep their numbers 
from dwindling any further.

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:01.840
Like cleaning the sand in beaches?

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:04.300
That's one of our activities.

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:09.970
A lot of sea turtles are put in danger 
because of human activity.

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:12.320
Human activity?

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:15.600
Their eggs get squashed 
by cars and people,

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:19.800
or they're attracted to artificial lights, 
which makes them lose their direction.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:22.460
Or large pieces of garbage 
get in the way of the young,

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:25.990
and they lose their lives 
trying to make it to the sea.

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:27.710
Oh, no...

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:29.950
After they're finally born into our world...

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:40.580
They struggle so hard to make
it to the sea with their tiny bodies.

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:45.310
Even if they make it back to the sea, 
there are other dangers lurking.

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:47.270
Marine pollution?

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:51.560
When we dissect sea turtles 
that had died and washed ashore,

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:55.320
we find artificial materials 
more often than not.

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:59.000
Last month, a sea turtle washed ashore 
and was tangled in rope.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:03.960
It's thought that only one
in 5,000 hatchlings survive,

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:07.600
but if that's just the way things go in nature, 
there's nothing to do about it.

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:11.480
But we want to stop them losing their lives 
because of human activities,

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:13.040
as much as we can.

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:17.880
I know that sounds really pretentious.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:21.240
At the end of the day, 
we just have to do what we can.

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:25.080
I had no idea, even though
I work at an aquarium.

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:26.800
No one does, at first.

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:29.820
You'll learn going forward.

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:33.810
Come back again sometime.

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:36.600
Your pork-and-egg rice balls were delicious.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.100
Thank you for taking care of us.

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:49.200
It doesn't have to be anything big, right?

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:51.940
As long as it helps the animals.

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:52.870
Yeah.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:59.630
I'm going to focus on my marketing work more, 
so that it helps the animals!

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:15.470
I'm very sorry!

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:18.280
I caused so much trouble.

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:20.030
I won't let it happen again.

00:06:20.030 --> 00:06:22.360
I will give my marketing work 
everything I have going forward!

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:23.980
Just do this for me.

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:25.980
<b>Tingarla Weddings</b>

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:25.980
<b>Project Proposal</b>

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:30.360
I'll have you leave the marketing department 
as soon as you're done with that job.

00:06:31.670 --> 00:06:33.280
Kukuru-san...

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:35.760
The attendants team has an opening.

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:36.790
I'll put in a recommendation.

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:40.040
Attendants...

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:42.010
Just focus on this job for now.

00:06:42.010 --> 00:06:45.800
I've negotiated with the wedding planners 
to schedule us for a meeting next Friday.

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:49.080
If we don't get the deal this time, 
that's it for this deal.

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:50.430
Understood.

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:54.110
Welcome back.

00:06:54.110 --> 00:06:55.000
Jeez.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.130
I thought you'd quit!

00:06:57.130 --> 00:06:59.320
Sorry I worried you.

00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:01.980
I couldn't answer your calls.

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:03.340
It's fine.

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:04.940
You're back safe now.

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:07.860
I get to poke your cheeks again.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:10.030
Also, the attendant team?

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:12.540
I don't know. It's all so sudden.

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:14.650
So you're being transferred, right?

00:07:14.650 --> 00:07:16.300
Good for you.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:20.060
You'll do better as an attendant 
than in marketing.

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:21.480
Right, Karin-san?

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:23.290
Y-Yeah.

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:27.210
Didn't you want to become
an attendant, too, Karin-chan?

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:29.340
I'm going to go talk 
to the assistant director.

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:31.420
Don't mind me.

00:07:31.420 --> 00:07:34.510
Just focus on the job 
in front of you.

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:40.670
Yeah, focus!

00:07:40.670 --> 00:07:41.350
Let's see...

00:07:50.370 --> 00:07:51.860
Fuuka-chan.

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:53.480
Good morning.

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:55.130
My wife told me.

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:56.660
You went to the island, huh?

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:00.880
I really wanted to see her, 
once she told me where she was.

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:03.020
Sorry for causing you 
so much trouble.

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:05.000
No, I'm glad I got to go.

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:10.960
I'm glad I'm back with Kukuru, of course, 
but I also got to see sea turtles hatch,

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:13.630
and Misaki-san told me 
some valuable information.

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:15.740
That's good, then.

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:19.560
Keep an eye on Kukuru-chan for us 
going forward, too.

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:23.050
She can be a bit perilous 
when she's on her own.

00:08:23.050 --> 00:08:24.200
You're right.

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:31.030
<b>Wedding Idea Notes

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:31.030
I came up with some ideas, but...

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:33.850
They're all way too much 
for the animals to deal with!

00:08:33.850 --> 00:08:35.780
I can't!

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:46.170
I'm sure a fish getting married
in an event like this would find real happiness.

00:08:47.070 --> 00:08:49.450
What's that supposed to mean?

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:51.160
Kukuru.

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:53.010
Ready to go home?

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:55.180
Fuuka!

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:59.180
<b>Please!</b>

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:59.180
<b>Always yield to the car on the right 
in the passing area.</b>

00:08:56.580 --> 00:08:59.180
Weddings, huh?

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:03.680
There isn't much we can do, 
if we care about the sea life first.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:08.440
I know the wedding is supposed 
to be for the newlyweds.

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:12.330
But it isn't an aquarium 
without the animals.

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:20.810
Ban-chan's still here.

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:21.830
Yeah.

00:09:23.780 --> 00:09:26.660
Hey, about the wedding project...

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:31.630
What would you think if the bride and groom 
were people you're close to?

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:33.290
People I'm close to?

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:35.390
Say...

00:09:35.390 --> 00:09:36.170
You!

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:37.720
Me?!

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:43.220
You'd be so pretty as a bride.

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:46.300
I'd take so many pretty photos!

00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:49.230
And I'd prepare lots of your favorite dishes,

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:53.690
and I'd make it a joyful ceremony 
from beginning to end.

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:56.170
Thanks.

00:09:56.170 --> 00:10:00.460
I feel like there's so much 
I'd want to do for you.

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:03.950
I wonder if Miura-san feels like this, too.

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:08.960
Does she care about the bride and groom 
as much as I care about animals?

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:11.460
I'm sure she does.

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:15.210
Oh yeah.

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:17.580
I might be transferring 
to the attendants team.

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:20.450
I'm not sure yet, though.

00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:23.240
It'll be great taking care 
of the animals together again.

00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:24.880
Choko's moving over, too.

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:26.140
I can't wait.

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:28.570
Choko's coming to Tingarla?!

00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:29.710
Yeah!

00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:30.640
Pretty soon.

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:32.440
Oh, man.

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:35.610
All right, I'm going to sprint 
to the presentation.

00:10:55.160 --> 00:10:56.910
Making progress, huh?

00:10:56.910 --> 00:11:01.420
Talking to Fuuka yesterday cleared my head.

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:03.550
It's important to ask people for advice.

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:07.030
It broadens your perspective, 
and it adds depth to your ideas.

00:11:07.030 --> 00:11:08.230
That's so true.

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:11.000
Oh, I should ask you, too.

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:14.110
What would you want if you were going 
to have your wedding at an aquarium?

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:16.680
I-I'm not sure.

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:19.800
I'm so busy thinking about work 
at the moment.

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:20.950
Really?

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:24.590
I thought about it overnight,

00:11:24.590 --> 00:11:27.160
but I'm going to put my name 
in for the attendant position.

00:11:29.950 --> 00:11:31.690
I gotta get to my meeting.

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:32.840
Good luck.

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:33.670
You, too.

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:39.670
Weddings huh?

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:42.430
I'd totally wear a mermaid dress.

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:45.430
My headdress and bouquet 
would be like corals.

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:49.560
My main condition is for Shizu-kun 
to enjoy it without getting bored.

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:51.140
Kids get bored easily.

00:11:51.450 --> 00:11:53.000
I see.

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:54.440
Thanks for the notes!

00:11:55.430 --> 00:11:56.650
Weddings?

00:11:57.020 --> 00:11:58.480
Why would you ask <i>me</i>?

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:01.080
It's for work. Help me out.

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:01.960
I can't.

00:12:02.390 --> 00:12:04.360
I'll answer in his place.

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:05.320
Tell me.

00:12:05.630 --> 00:12:09.290
First, the invitation cards 
are definitely blue-whale themed.

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:13.680
I'd distribute fish trivia 
and quiz questions.

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:16.540
Those who get it right get konbu 
and bonito flakes.

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:17.500
For the bomboniere...

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:19.500
<b>Wedding Idea Notes V2

00:12:27.170 --> 00:12:28.280
Kukuru.

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:29.660
What's up?

00:12:29.660 --> 00:12:30.970
Do you have a moment?

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:35.550
Sorry, I have to have the assistant director 
look at my project proposal.

00:12:35.550 --> 00:12:36.270
Is it urgent?

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:38.520
Nah, next time, then.

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:39.760
Break a leg.

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:40.680
Yeah.

00:12:48.930 --> 00:12:49.840
Very well.

00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:50.970
Let's go with this.

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:52.140
Okay!

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:54.280
Email it to the wedding planners as well.

00:12:54.280 --> 00:12:55.120
Okay.

00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:58.210
Um, about the presentation...

00:12:58.590 --> 00:12:59.460
What?

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:04.390
I'd like to bring Miura-san 
over here to Tingarla.

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:06.970
<b>Ready to Return</b>

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:15.640
<b>The Pacific Garbage Patch</b>

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:17.980
Huh, what a surprise.

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:20.720
Miyazawa-san, are you interested 
in environmental issues?

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:23.740
I had an opportunity to learn 
about the garbage issue.

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:25.700
I want to learn more about it.

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:30.140
Ocean pollution is one of the problems, 
but there's a ton more, too.

00:13:30.140 --> 00:13:33.290
For example, the rise of sea temperatures 
as a result of climate change

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:34.830
is the cause of a lot of crises.

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:37.290
The coral?

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:38.200
Yeah.

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:40.350
They're bleaching.

00:13:40.350 --> 00:13:45.010
Once coral bleaches, it never recovers, 
and it eventually dies.

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:49.930
The coral reefs in Miyako City, where I'm from, 
are dwindling really fast, too.

00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:53.270
I want to save them as much as I can 
while they're still alive.

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:11.630
We were looking forward to seeing you.

00:14:11.630 --> 00:14:14.240
Thank you for taking time to come.

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:16.120
Sorry for calling you out 
all the way here.

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:18.420
I was surprised, 
because it was so sudden.

00:14:18.730 --> 00:14:23.300
We really wanted you to see
the marine life as part of our pitch.

00:14:23.610 --> 00:14:26.660
Could you show me around, then?

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:28.300
I don't want to waste time.

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:30.360
This way, please.

00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:36.770
This tank offers a view of creatures 
in the Okinawa area.

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:40.270
There are all kinds 
of colorful and adorable fish.

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:44.270
That awesome-looking fish is a giant grouper.

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:47.720
They get to be up 
to nearly three meters!

00:14:47.720 --> 00:14:50.730
There are even legends 
that they've swallowed humans.

00:14:54.670 --> 00:14:57.290
The jellyfish are popular 
for making people feel better.

00:14:57.630 --> 00:15:02.460
The gentle way they drift 
has a relaxing effect.

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:04.290
That's plenty.

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:07.300
Was I not called here 
for the project pitch?

00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:09.400
Right.

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:10.550
Then...

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:19.560
This is the wedding venue: 
the White Sand Dome.

00:15:20.370 --> 00:15:24.810
We're still setting up the interior, 
but we plan to be open by next week.

00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:28.280
I'd like to check on several points.

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:29.820
What about photography?

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:35.970
We'll hire professionals 
to take memorable photos.

00:15:35.970 --> 00:15:36.990
The meals?

00:15:36.990 --> 00:15:41.330
We'll prepare receptions as requested 
at our restaurant.

00:15:42.130 --> 00:15:45.660
You seemed preoccupied 
with protecting the animals last time.

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:48.270
The fact that we care 
about the animals hasn't changed.

00:15:48.270 --> 00:15:51.470
But the wedding is the primary
objective of the event.

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:57.600
We want to find a middle ground, 
so that the clients can be satisfied as well.

00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:01.710
Then we can't back down 
on having decorations.

00:16:01.710 --> 00:16:04.110
We'd like to keep them to a minimum.

00:16:04.110 --> 00:16:06.160
That would appear too bleak.

00:16:06.160 --> 00:16:09.860
We don't believe we would
need flashy decorations here.

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:11.550
And why would that be?

00:16:11.550 --> 00:16:13.640
Have a look up at the ceiling!

00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:19.880
From top to bottom, 
you're surrounded by a dome aquarium.

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:24.370
Brilliantly colored fish will be swimming 
in the sparkling water.

00:16:24.680 --> 00:16:28.810
I believe it will be plenty gorgeous, 
even without decorations!

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:33.560
We'll also be covering the ground 
with white sand,

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:35.710
which will light the room 
all the way down to your feet.

00:16:35.710 --> 00:16:37.050
Sand?

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:38.100
What about shoes?

00:16:38.380 --> 00:16:39.610
No shoes.

00:16:39.610 --> 00:16:41.060
It'll be a barefoot wedding!

00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:45.360
There was nothing about this 
on the proposal!

00:16:45.360 --> 00:16:47.190
Barefoot is taking it too far.

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:51.080
The aquarium extends all the way 
to the sand.

00:16:51.080 --> 00:16:55.700
All around you, you're surrounded by life, 
as you celebrate the newlyweds.

00:16:56.140 --> 00:16:58.410
Don't you think that would be fantastic?

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:01.760
It's like having a wedding under the sea.

00:17:01.760 --> 00:17:06.300
I'm sure any couple 
that loves the ocean would love this!

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:12.900
I've never seen or even heard 
of such a wedding.

00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:19.030
But that makes it all the more intriguing!

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:24.980
There's still plenty of things to consider, 
and some adjustments will be necessary.

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:27.900
But I think it would be worth trying.

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:29.900
Do you mean...

00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:32.980
Let's make Tingarla Weddings happen.

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:37.530
Thank you!

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:37.530
We're honored.

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:40.940
I'm so glad I came to Tingarla today.

00:17:41.840 --> 00:17:44.670
There was a lot that I couldn't get 
out of just reading the proposal.

00:17:44.670 --> 00:17:47.320
Seeing the fish and the new area in person

00:17:47.320 --> 00:17:49.250
has given me a better idea 
of what it will look like.

00:17:49.990 --> 00:17:51.250
Right!

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:54.650
Misakino-san, 
do you have some time afterwards?

00:17:54.650 --> 00:17:56.800
I'd like to learn more 
about the other fish.

00:17:56.800 --> 00:17:59.520
It might be useful to know 
for the weddings.

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:00.790
Of course!

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:20.910
I'll come again.

00:18:27.970 --> 00:18:28.840
Plankton.

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:29.420
Yes?

00:18:30.980 --> 00:18:31.920
Well done.

00:18:34.160 --> 00:18:35.820
Thank you.

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:42.490
Cheers!

00:18:48.640 --> 00:18:50.410
That hits the spot!

00:18:50.410 --> 00:18:53.690
I've never had such good Okinawan lime juice!

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:57.720
I haven't seen Kukuru so happy 
in a long time.

00:18:57.720 --> 00:18:59.560
Your proposal went through, right?

00:18:59.560 --> 00:19:00.530
Congrats!

00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:02.480
That's amazing!

00:19:02.480 --> 00:19:03.950
I knew you could do it.

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:07.360
Miura-san bought a jellyfish plushie.

00:19:07.360 --> 00:19:09.240
She said she'll show it off at home.

00:19:09.890 --> 00:19:10.960
That's great.

00:19:11.230 --> 00:19:15.310
She had no interest at first, 
but she fell in love after.

00:19:15.310 --> 00:19:20.340
Even more people might fall in love 
with animals, if the weddings work out.

00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:22.320
I hope it happens.

00:19:22.320 --> 00:19:24.990
Yeah. I have to work hard 
to make it happen.

00:19:24.990 --> 00:19:28.010
I thought you're transferring, 
though, Kukuru-san.

00:19:29.220 --> 00:19:31.560
Aren't you becoming an attendant?

00:19:32.820 --> 00:19:35.670
I was so busy with the project 
that I forgot.

00:19:37.750 --> 00:19:40.490
I applied to be an attendant, too.

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:42.350
Wow, it's happening, huh?

00:19:42.350 --> 00:19:43.500
That's beautiful.

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:45.630
You've always dreamed 
of becoming an attendant.

00:19:45.630 --> 00:19:46.510
Yeah.

00:19:46.510 --> 00:19:48.160
It's a rare opportunity.

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:49.750
I didn't want to regret not doing it.

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:51.500
You're awesome.

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:54.790
It takes courage to do something new.

00:19:54.790 --> 00:19:56.890
What did the assistant director say?

00:19:56.890 --> 00:20:00.170
He looked really dissatisfied at first.

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:01.740
But he said he'll think about it.

00:20:01.740 --> 00:20:03.300
Thank goodness.

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:04.810
I see.

00:20:04.810 --> 00:20:08.100
It's going to be either Kukuru or Karin-chan 
who's taking over for Kai.

00:20:09.200 --> 00:20:10.220
Kai?

00:20:10.920 --> 00:20:14.220
My mom heard from a Kamee customer...

00:20:14.220 --> 00:20:16.780
Kai's dad collapsed.

00:20:19.510 --> 00:20:21.020
Do you have a moment?

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:23.740
Nah, next time, then.

00:20:23.740 --> 00:20:24.950
Break a leg.

00:20:25.640 --> 00:20:26.870
Kai...

00:20:28.200 --> 00:20:30.430
Sorry, Fuuka, I'll pay you back later!

00:20:30.430 --> 00:20:31.790
Kukuru!

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:32.960
<b>Nakamura Kai</b>

00:20:51.010 --> 00:20:52.140
There.

00:20:52.720 --> 00:20:53.600
Kai!

00:20:54.840 --> 00:20:55.660
Kukuru.

00:20:58.100 --> 00:21:00.120
I heard about your dad.

00:21:00.120 --> 00:21:01.110
Is he okay?

00:21:01.470 --> 00:21:02.790
Oh, yeah.

00:21:03.170 --> 00:21:05.210
He needs surgery.

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:07.990
I don't think I'll be able 
to work for a while.

00:21:08.350 --> 00:21:09.700
I see.

00:21:10.630 --> 00:21:12.500
Are you quitting work here?

00:21:12.800 --> 00:21:14.560
Don't make that face.

00:21:14.560 --> 00:21:15.770
I'm not quitting anymore.

00:21:15.770 --> 00:21:17.340
Just going on leave.

00:21:18.080 --> 00:21:22.160
The director told me to come back 
once my family's all right.

00:21:22.160 --> 00:21:24.080
I never knew.

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:25.260
Thank goodness.

00:21:25.950 --> 00:21:28.620
Take care of the animals 
for me until then.

00:21:29.630 --> 00:21:32.640
I'll feel safe if you're the one doing it.

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:36.280
Shit!

00:21:36.280 --> 00:21:38.800
I have to head home.

00:21:38.800 --> 00:21:41.150
I hope your dad gets better soon.

00:21:41.150 --> 00:21:42.330
Thanks.

00:21:42.330 --> 00:21:43.650
Later!
